@startuml
' What: how one hexagram line gets its value at the generation change (D-48, D-49).
' Shows: body reading x -> normalised b -> blended with pressure p into the line score s;
'        the sign (yin / yang) has a hysteresis band, the old threshold decides whether the line trembles.
' Source: brainstorming-base.md, D-48, D-49, Appendix D.3. All constants (k, x0, w, h, threshold) are playtest values.
title Line score of one line (D-48, D-49)
start
:Body reading x for this axis;
:b = tanh(k * (x - x0));
:Pressure p piled up this generation;
:s = w * b + (1 - w) * p   (w about 0.7);
if (s beyond the hysteresis band h,\non the other side of the current sign?) then (yes)
  :Sign flips (yin <-> yang);
else (no)
  :Sign stays;
endif
if (|s| close to the old threshold?) then (yes)
  :Dice decide old or young,\nweighted by distance;
elseif (|s| above the old threshold?) then (yes)
  :Old line = trembling line;
else (below)
  :Young line = stable;
endif
stop
@enduml
